# Fitting data

A spring tested at five loads.

```calc
F := [0; 50; 100; 150; 200]*1 N
x := [0.0; 2.1; 3.9; 6.2; 7.9]*1 mm
```

The stiffness, from the least-squares line, and how straight the data is:

```calc
k := slope(x, F) = ? N/mm
F0 := intercept(x, F) = ?
corr(x, F) = ?
```

The load at 5 mm, read off the data three ways:

```calc
linterp(x, F, 5 mm) = ?
interp(cspline(x, F), x, F, 5 mm) = ?
interp(regress(x, F, 2), x, F, 5 mm) = ?
```

A fit of chosen terms, and the roots of a cubic:

```calc
f(t) := [1; t; t^2]
linfit(x, F, f) = ?
polyroots([-6; 11; -6; 1]) = ?
Stdev(F) = ?
```
